{%- comment -%}
  ces-img — one responsive <img> for the ces-* sections.

  Every ces section used to write its own `<img src="{{ image | image_url:
  width: 1600 }}">`. That ships one desktop-sized file to every phone: a
  390px screen downloaded the 1600px copy of each picture and threw most of
  the pixels away. A srcset plus a `sizes` describing the slot lets the
  browser pick, and the intrinsic width/height keep the page from jumping as
  each one lands.

  Accepts:
    - image     {Image}   required; nothing is rendered without one
    - sizes     {String}  CSS width of the slot, e.g.
                          '(min-width: 750px) 40vw, 100vw'. Default '100vw'.
    - max       {Number}  widest source worth generating. Default 1600.
    - alt       {String}
    - class     {String}
    - eager     {Boolean} true for a picture above the fold — it then loads
                          straight away instead of waiting for the scroll
    - priority  {Boolean} fetchpriority="high"; use on the LCP image only

  The shape is left to the section: they set aspect-ratio and object-fit in
  their own CSS, so cropping here would only fight them.

  Filters are not allowed in {% render %} arguments, so assign first:
    {%- assign img_alt = block.settings.title | escape -%}
    {% render 'ces-img', image: block.settings.image, alt: img_alt,
       sizes: '(min-width: 750px) 25vw, 80vw', max: 800 %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if image != blank -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign ces_img_max = max | default: 1600

    comment
      Only the steps up to `max` — asking Shopify for a source wider than the
      slot ever gets is what this snippet exists to stop.
    endcomment
    assign ces_img_pool = '160,240,320,420,540,680,860,1080,1280,1600,1920,2200' | split: ','
    assign ces_img_widths = ''
    for ces_img_w in ces_img_pool
      assign ces_img_n = ces_img_w | times: 1
      if ces_img_n <= ces_img_max
        if ces_img_widths == blank
          assign ces_img_widths = ces_img_w
        else
          assign ces_img_widths = ces_img_widths | append: ',' | append: ces_img_w
        endif
      endif
    endfor
    if ces_img_widths == blank
      assign ces_img_widths = ces_img_max | append: ''
    endif

    assign ces_img_loading = 'lazy'
    if eager
      assign ces_img_loading = 'eager'
    endif

    assign ces_img_priority = 'auto'
    if priority
      assign ces_img_priority = 'high'
    endif

    assign ces_img_sizes = sizes | default: '100vw'
    assign ces_img_alt = alt | default: image.alt | escape
    assign ces_img_class = class | default: ''
  -%}
  {{
    image
    | image_url: width: ces_img_max
    | image_tag:
      loading: ces_img_loading,
      fetchpriority: ces_img_priority,
      decoding: 'async',
      sizes: ces_img_sizes,
      widths: ces_img_widths,
      class: ces_img_class,
      alt: ces_img_alt
  }}
{%- endif -%}
